{"key": "KXRECBASELINE|Will the Republican reconcilliation bill be scored relative to a current policy baseline?|If the Congressional Budget Office scoring documents evaluate the next reconciliation bill that becomes law relative to a current policy, rather than current law, baseline, then the market resolves to Yes.", "decision": "NO", "confidence": 0.95, "reasoning": "The Republican reconciliation bill (H.R. 1) was signed into law on July 4, 2025. The Congressional Budget Office's primary official scoring documents evaluated this bill relative to a current law baseline, not a current policy baseline. While Republicans requested and received an alternative scoring using a current policy baseline, the CBO's primary scoring methodology used the traditional current law baseline approach. The resolution criteria requires that \"the Congressional Budget Office scoring documents evaluate the next reconciliation bill that becomes law relative to a current policy, rather than current law, baseline.\" Since the official CBO scoring documents used current law baseline as their primary methodology, the market resolves to NO.", "sources": ["https://www.aabb.org/news-resources/news/article/2025/07/09/trump-signs-2025-budget-reconciliation-bill--enacting-sweeping-changes-to-health-programs", "https://www.cpapracticeadvisor.com/2025/06/29/republican-senate-tax-bill-would-add-3-3-trillion-to-deficit-says-cbo/163933/", "https://www.dailysignal.com/2025/06/04/price-tag-big-beautiful-bill-revealed/"], "queries": ["Republican reconciliation bill 2025 2026 CBO scoring baseline", "Republican reconciliation bill passed law 2025 current policy baseline CBO", "\"reconciliation bill\" Trump signed into law 2025", "CBO official scoring Republican tax bill reconciliation current law baseline July 2025"], "links": ["https://www.dailysignal.com/?p=63448", "https://www.dailysignal.com/2025/06/04/price-tag-big-beautiful-bill-revealed/", "https://www.medicarerights.org/?p=36511", "https://www.asao